{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel did, etc.</b> It is difficult: what is the place of ״וּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל עָשׂוּ״ etc., after it already said ״וַיּוֹצִיאוּ אֶת הַמְקַלֵּל״ etc. ״וַיִּרְגְּמוּ אֹתוֹ אָבֶן״ — do I not see that they did what HaShem commanded? And one may say: since the matter came about through a quarrel and dispute that was between the Israelite man and the son of the Israelite woman, there is room to say that they carried out the written judgment upon him also out of lingering resentment in the heart. Therefore it says <b>they did as HaShem commanded</b> — meaning, it was for the sake of HaShem's command that they did it." "<b>Or</b> the verse intends to elevate the mitzvah they performed to the account of all Israel, even though not all of them had a hand in it." "<b>Or</b> it further intends: through this deed, by which they avenged the honor of His blessed Name, the verse elevates them as though they had fulfilled the entire Torah — and this is what it says, ״כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה ה׳ אֶת מֹשֶׁה״, in a general sense." "<b>Or</b> it may say in this manner: since in HaShem's command to Moses He said <b>הוֹצֵא אֶת הַמְקַלֵּל</b>, which refers back to Moses, that he would take him out, and the stoning would be performed by Israel, as it is written <b>וְרָגְמוּ אֹתוֹ כָּל הָעֵדָה</b>, whereas here it says ״וַיּוֹצִיאוּ הַמְקַלֵּל״, which refers back to Israel mentioned just above — the verse comes to praise Israel and says <b>and the children of Israel did as HaShem commanded Moses</b>, meaning: as for taking him out, they preceded Moses and did it before Moses did, out of zeal and alacrity to fulfill HaShem's command. And according to the earlier interpretations, הוֹצֵא may be explained as: either he himself or his agent." "<b>Thus concludes the parashah of Emor.</b>"], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:00:49.287902156Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}